build: 2026-06-23 v10.62.0 (Header Dual-Monitor — live EKG + immersive monitor in the persistent top bar)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notes: Founder idea (screenshot, red-1/red-2): the persistent header corners become two live monitors — LEFT a small EKG-style control trace of the live pulse, RIGHT a monitor of the immersive visualisation; the first building block of the DMMW multiscreen / livestream / projection-mapping output. Built to full quality, NO stub: the EKG is a pure SwiftUI Canvas over the real bandpass-filtered rPPG waveform (cameraRPPG.waveform) + live BPM (cheap, no GPU, flash-safe); the immersive monitor reuses the REAL MetalBioView, rendered only while a bio session is live to bound GPU. Both sit in WorkspaceView.topBar (above every surface — Arrange/Clips/Compose) and tap-expand to a full-screen monitor (big BPM + EKG + coaching, or the full immersive visual) with a close control — the seam where an external display / stream output plugs in next. Fully VoiceOver-labelled (label/value/hint/isButton), Uncodixfy-compliant (solid fills, 1px borders, ≤12px radius, no glow, opacity-only). New: HeaderMonitors.swift (PulseTrace, PulseMonitorMini, ImmersiveMonitorMini, ExpandedMonitorView); WorkspaceView.topBar rewired. Cumulative with the v10.61 stop-hang stability fix and the confirmed-working rPPG lock. iOS compile gate validates the SwiftUI + Metal.
